 Arrays in Java
An array in Java is a collection of elements of the same data type stored under a single variable name. Each element is accessed using an index starting from 0.
1. Types of Arrays
Type	Description	Example
One-Dimensional Array	Stores elements in a single sequence	int[] a = {10, 20, 30};
Two-Dimensional Array	Stores elements in rows and columns	int[][] a = {{1, 2}, {3, 4}};
Multidimensional Array	Uses three or more dimensions	int[][][] a = new int[2][3][4];
Jagged Array	Rows can have different lengths	int[][] a = {{1, 2}, {3, 4, 5}};

2. Array Declaration and Initialization
Declaration:
int[] arr;


Memory allocation:
arr = new int[5];


Declaration with initialization:
int[] arr = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};


Accessing elements:
System.out.println(arr[0]); // 10
System.out.println(arr[2]); // 30


3. Array Operations and Methods – Category Wise
Unlike String, Java arrays have very few built-in members. Most array utility methods are provided by the java.util.Arrays class.
A. Array Length and Access
Operation	Description	Example
arr.length	Returns array length	arr.length
arr[index]	Accesses an element	arr[2]
arr[index] = value	Updates an element	arr[1] = 100

B. Array Sorting Methods
Method	Description
Arrays.sort()	Sorts array elements
Arrays.parallelSort()	Sorts using a parallel sorting algorithm when appropriate

C. Array Searching Methods
Method	Description
Arrays.binarySearch()	Searches a sorted array
Arrays.mismatch()	Finds the first mismatching index between arrays

D. Array Comparison Methods
Method	Description
Arrays.equals()	Compares array elements
Arrays.deepEquals()	Compares nested arrays recursively
Arrays.compare()	Compares arrays lexicographically
Arrays.deepHashCode()	Computes a hash code for nested arrays

E. Array Copying Methods
Method	Description
Arrays.copyOf()	Copies an array to a specified length
Arrays.copyOfRange()	Copies a specified range
System.arraycopy()	Copies elements between arrays
clone()	Creates a shallow copy of an array

F. Array Filling and Updating Methods
Method	Description
Arrays.fill()	Fills array elements with a value
Arrays.setAll()	Sets elements using a generator function
Arrays.parallelSetAll()	Sets elements using parallel computation

G. Array Conversion Methods
Method	Description
Arrays.toString()	Converts a one-dimensional array to readable text
Arrays.deepToString()	Converts nested arrays to readable text
Arrays.asList()	Creates a fixed-size list backed by an object array
Arrays.stream()	Creates a stream from supported array types



 Java String Methods – Category Wise
Java String methods can be divided into 10 categories based on their functionality.
1. String Length and Character Access Methods
Used to find the length of a string and access individual characters.
Method	Description
length()	Returns the number of characters
charAt(index)	Returns the character at the specified index
toCharArray()	Converts a string into a character array
getChars()	Copies characters into an array

2. String Comparison Methods
Used to compare two strings.
Method	Description
equals()	Compares string contents
equalsIgnoreCase()	Compares strings ignoring case
compareTo()	Compares strings lexicographically
compareToIgnoreCase()	Compares lexicographically ignoring case
contentEquals()	Compares with another character sequence
regionMatches()	Compares specific portions of strings

3. String Searching Methods
Used to search for characters or substrings.
Method	Description
indexOf()	Finds the first occurrence
lastIndexOf()	Finds the last occurrence
contains()	Checks whether a substring exists
startsWith()	Checks the beginning of a string
endsWith()	Checks the ending of a string
matches()	Checks whether a string matches a regular expression

4. String Modification Methods
Used to create modified versions of strings.
Method	Description
toUpperCase()	Converts to uppercase
toLowerCase()	Converts to lowercase
replace()	Replaces characters or substrings
replaceAll()	Replaces matches of a regular expression
replaceFirst()	Replaces the first regex match
trim()	Removes leading and trailing characters up to U+0020
strip()	Removes leading and trailing whitespace
stripLeading()	Removes leading whitespace
stripTrailing()	Removes trailing whitespace

5. String Extraction Methods
Used to extract parts of strings.
Method	Description
substring(start)	Extracts from the starting index
substring(start, end)	Extracts between two indices
subSequence(start, end)	Returns a character subsequence

6. String Concatenation and Joining Methods
Used to combine strings.
Method	Description
concat()	Joins two strings
join()	Joins multiple strings with a delimiter
format()	Creates a formatted string

7. String Splitting Methods
Used to divide strings into multiple parts.
Method	Description
split()	Splits a string using a regular expression
splitWithDelimiters()	Splits while retaining delimiters in the result
lines()	Returns a stream of lines

8. String Validation Methods
Used to check whether strings are empty or blank.
Method	Description
isEmpty()	Checks whether string length is zero
isBlank()	Checks whether a string is empty or contains only whitespace

9. String Conversion Methods
Used to convert values or strings into other representations.
Method	Description
valueOf()	Converts different data types into strings
copyValueOf()	Converts a character array into a string
getBytes()	Converts a string into a byte array
toCharArray()	Converts a string into a character array

10. Other Useful String Methods
Method	Description
repeat()	Repeats a string multiple times
intern()	Returns the canonical representation from the string pool
hashCode()	Returns the string's hash code
toString()	Returns the string itself
indent()	Adjusts indentation of lines
stripIndent()	Removes incidental indentation
